Fort Ludious is of no advantage except that it has several dragons that
you can eat. Go in with a ring of conflict, lock yourself behind a door,
and let the army kill themselves swarming around you. Really at this point
in the game there is nothing you can use the gold from the vault to buy
that is useful, and it's probably more efficent to go wraith hunting to
go up a few levels than killing millions of low level characters. I'd
bypass it.

Oh, the soldiers are also a good source of C and K rations, so I went in with
a bag and swept up on food. 

Do the quest, get the object and the book of the dead, and try to get both 
teleport and teleport control as intrinsics (Will help much in maze levels).
Note the square you enter the quest at since this will be how you teleport out
(Quest Leader will now ignore you). Now charge down and go for the
amulet. Also eat lots of giants to get your strength up... a tinning kit
is useful since giants make you satiated quickly. Questionable how useful
the Dwarvish mines are since the luckstone seems fairly pointless;
may want to bypass them also. 


